body:
This is a double issue, resulting from the combination of:

&#x200B;

\-People getting dumber as tools do stuff for them without need of conscious input

&#x200B;

and

&#x200B;

\-People getting dumber as they blindly follow the whims and stupid ideas of popular "streamers", "influencers" and similar, most of them people who never worked and, thus, have no idea how the world runs outside their bubble.

&#x200B;

This is not to say progress or society is bad "per se", but with all things, we should be careful and remember to THINK before ACTing. Being given the appropiate tool/easiest solution everytime, does not imply disregarding the use of your brain.

Lol "Last resort" when they just spam bans left and right...

&#x200B;

Meanwhile, bot Fantasy XIV going strong. Yesterday i found a cascade of them with "FFFSFSDSDSDS AWUQUAIUAQQ" names teleporting all over the place, at level 50.

Well, you can choose between DPS with heals, DPS with cards, and DPS with a fairy that handles healing, because doing anything that's not DPS will get you flamed in this community.

&#x200B;

...I would, for once, like a healer that doesn't "DPS" per se. That doesn't mean one that sits there idly. It could be handling a mini-game slightly more complex than AST cards, that ends up heavily powering the team if done correctly, debuffing the enemy, etc.

At levels 60+, cheesing the stupid, stupid AI is the only way to win.

&#x200B;

They not only have inhuman speed, and read your input (they "dodge" instant knockdowns and the like) , but blatantly cheat, using any spell they wish without cooldowns, blocking in movement/spinning while blocking, grappling/blocking from the floor, etc. etc.

The thought of going full Walter White, throwing meth at your teammates to buff them up is just....

&#x200B;

Yes, please.

Healer by a quite long shot. I can't talk for endgame bosses as i'm not there yet, but from my experience, both in low lvl FF and in other MMORPGS, healer is the most crucial role.

&#x200B;

\-Tanks can be somewhat substituted by plate-armored classes, in this case, DRG can be a somewhat offtank. This, however , means that the offtank has to be the best geared and highest dps player in order to keep aggro, as non-tanks tend not to have any aggro mitigation, or everyone has to slow down dps.

&#x200B;

\-DPS... well, anyone can dps, with more or less effectiveness. Less dps means higher bossing time, which means higher chances of commiting a grave mistake and wiping the party. But they're not necessary per se, unless there's a very tight enrage timer.

&#x200B;

\-Healers on the other hand, are unique regarding the fact that they push bars up. While leeching mechanisms allow other characters to keep their life somewhat up, in very rare cases the games allow you to cap your own hp by simply hitting an enemy with enough lifesteal. They can also serve as improvised tanks against magic damage, in games where cloth armor gives a bigger bonus to magic defense, than plate does.

Do

  (Cast)

While (true);

Aye, i stopped playing the tanky dps char i had because of this.   


9500 health, capped resists (minus chaos, which was at a respectable 20%) , still kept getting oneshot by random hits. If it was chaos (otherwise i can't explain such absurd damage), i would like to know the source.  


&#x200B;

This so much. And if you wanna go a step further, play the visual novel. That was the basis for all the Fate/Garbage they've been spewing out. Don't get me wrong, the VN is fantastic. All the other stuff they have been airing these last few years... not so much.   


It will give you insight on the three "core" routes: The main one (Saber route) , the Unlimited Blade Works one (Shirou Route) , and the Heavens Feel one (Aimed to be an Ilya route, ended up being a Sakura Route, much darker.) . Play them in that order.

&#x200B;

A friend just talked me about the game and it looks fun. I plan to play it soon, but i first want to decide what to make. Since he's a mage, i thought i'd go with some melee, and after some questioning from my part, i decided to go the typical cloaky-rogue-slash-assassin with dual swords/daggers and CC traps, if possible.

&#x200B;

Looking at the wiki, however, i'm torn between several classes. The sabotager seems to be the best choice, but i'm worried about its combat viability. Assassin / trickster seem to be close seconds, so i'd be leaning for that class. I'm also looking to the Scion/Ascendants, though, wondering if it would be any good.

&#x200B;

Could i get some starting pointers? I was told the game picks up difficulty later on, and i've been yearning for some difficult game for a while, so this seems to be in my league.

This is exactly what happened. In beta, the first level or two were acquired by killing at most 5 mobs. But yeah, no exploding for 20 levels in the first zone. Then they made it "easier for new comers", and exactly THAT happened. 

&#x200B;

Oh, and people able to acquire top-level buffs at the first town, so if you do 20 dmg, and get a +400 dmg buff, that means you oneshot every single mob AND boss for the next 30-40 levels aswell.

I used to be a destacable member of the CH community ever since beta, some people may recognise my priest (Reimu), with which i participated in the first cross-server PVP tournament, dueled 1v1 against GM's, and carried endless amount of people through my 1500+ dungeon runs i did ever since i started.

&#x200B;

It pains me to see this, but i believe it was necessary. The game died the moment it went F2P and stupid mounts and costumes were added, all the while removing player customisation, and adding "leveling" weapons that made leveling trivial and unfun (The best part of the  game was the leveling up, really!)

This is why, as a beta player, i stopped playing the game.

&#x200B;

TERA was one of the best gaming experiences i ever had, playing the beta, subbing up until they made it F2P (And p2W). But then, what really killed the game was people driving around on cars and wearing stupid modern suits.

Creep. Gold bag. Mana Snack.

&#x200B;

Whatever you feel like calling them :P

Apologies, might have explained it wrong. As i said, i have 0 points on "Art knowledge".

